From 2848c2db6d86ff0ca20af4fc146597536dd549b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Igor Bogani <alessio.bogani@elettra.eu>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 16:31:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Adapt powerpcspe backend to GCC 15 API changes

Forward-port the out-of-tree PowerPC SPE (e500) target backend from
GCC 13.4 to GCC 15.2.  Applies to the two preceding cherry-picks that
reintroduced the backend from the GCC 8 era and fixed an SPE vec_perm
ICE; both arrive cleanly on top of releases/gcc-15 but the middle-end
API has moved on, and the target no longer builds without the
following adjustments.

API adaptations in gcc/config/powerpcspe/:

- powerpcspe.h: FLOAT_TYPE_SIZE, DOUBLE_TYPE_SIZE and LONG_DOUBLE_TYPE_SIZE
  are poisoned in GCC 15 system.h; remove the #define's and implement
  TARGET_C_MODE_FOR_FLOATING_TYPE (rs6000_c_mode_for_floating_type) in
  powerpcspe.cc, mirroring the rs6000 GCC 15 implementation: DFmode or
  TFmode for TI_LONG_DOUBLE_TYPE depending on rs6000_long_double_type_size,
  default_mode_for_floating_type otherwise.

- powerpcspe.cc: rs6000_md_asm_adjust now takes an additional
  vec<rtx> &uses parameter between constraints and clobbers
  (TARGET_MD_ASM_ADJUST signature change).

- powerpcspe.cc: rs6000_legitimate_address_p (and the debug wrapper)
  gain a trailing code_helper argument, defaulted to ERROR_MARK, per
  the TARGET_LEGITIMATE_ADDRESS_P signature change.  SPE ignores it.

- powerpcspe.cc: the attribute table is now a scoped_attribute_specs.
  Rename rs6000_attribute_table to rs6000_gnu_attributes, wrap it in
  rs6000_gnu_attribute_table, and expose the new
  rs6000_attribute_table[] array of scoped_attribute_specs pointers,
  following the rs6000 layout.

- powerpcspe-c.cc / powerpcspe-protos.h: altivec_resolve_overloaded_builtin
  gains a trailing bool parameter; give it a default value of false in
  the declaration so the numerous intra-file recursive call sites do
  not need to be touched.

Build-system adaptation:

- Add stub .opt.urls files for every .opt file under
  gcc/config/powerpcspe/ (476, aix64, darwin, linux64, powerpcspe,
  powerpcspe-tables, sysv4, xilinx).  GCC 15's Makefile requires
  <foo>.opt.urls for each <foo>.opt listed in extra_opt_files; we are
  an out-of-tree fork with no corresponding invoke.texi sections, so
  empty stubs (a single comment line) are the correct content.

Verified end-to-end:

  ../configure --target=powerpc-linux-gnuspe --enable-languages=c \
               --disable-multilib --disable-bootstrap \
               --without-headers --with-cpu=8548
  make all-gcc

produces xgcc (GCC) 15.2.1 and cc1.  Smoke tests pass:
  * hello.c emits valid PowerPC assembly;
  * double f(double, double) emits efdadd / efdmul with the ABI
    passing doubles in GPR pairs (r3,r9) per E500ABIUG;
  * a SLP-vectorizable vec_perm kernel on v2si compiles without the
    ICE fixed by the preceding cherry-pick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
